## UBE2M / KD-vs-control direction (accepted fact from the plan round)
UBE2M cannot be located: the file has no symbol column, and the ENSMUSG ID held in memory
for mouse Ube2m is absent — as are Actb and Ube2c, so the annotation version cannot be
trusted for ID guessing. Group direction therefore stays unresolved.
Direction is only weakly relevant: with the |log2FC| > 1 filter the test statistic is
invariant to which group is the baseline. Measured: refitting with K and W swapped gives
Spearman(p, p_swapped) = 0.9957, and 686/719 candidates shared (Jaccard 0.946); the small
residual difference is numerical (35 genes whose dispersion MLE sits on a flat/boundary
region), not conceptual.

## DE layer that WAS executed (equivalent implementation, clearly labelled)
`analysis/deseq_lite.py` re-implements: median-of-ratios size factors, gene-wise NB2
dispersion MLE (log-grid + refinement), parametric dispersion trend, EB shrinkage of
log-dispersion toward the trend, Wald test on the W-vs-K coefficient, BH adjustment, and
LFC shrinkage under a zero-centred normal prior with EM-estimated sd
(== `lfcShrink(type="normal")`; apeglm unavailable offline).

Validation evidence:
* NB profile NLL matches `scipy.stats.nbinom.logpmf` to < 1e-12.
* gene-wise dispersion vs independent scipy MLE: median |log difference| = 0.0005.
* BH matches `statsmodels.multipletests(method="fdr_bh")` to 2e-16.
* log2FC vs naive normalised-mean log-ratio: Spearman/corr ~0.83-0.94 on expressed genes.
* p-value calibration: using the TRUE dispersion gives p<0.05 in 5.3% of expressed genes
  (correct); with 3-vs-3 re-estimated dispersions the rate inflates to 13.4% for both the
  Wald and the LRT (dispersion MLE downward bias, not the reference distribution:
  a t-reference with df=2 over-corrects to 1.0%). A bootstrap-calibrated dispersion
  inflation factor of 2.2 restores the nominal rate (4.8-5.6%).

Filter funnel (contrast W vs K, K = baseline, disp_inflate = 2.2):
```
21884 total genes
  -> 11637  baseMean > 10
  ->  3488  and p-value < 0.05
  ->   719  and |shrunk log2FC| > 1     <-- candidate set (221 higher in W, 498 lower)
  alt: 1127 with |RAW log2FC| > 1; shrinkage removes 408, adds 0
  padj<0.05 variant: 719 (identical)
```
LFC shrinkage prior sd = 0.678; median disp_SHR (baseMean>10) = 0.0714.
Cross-check of the candidate set against log2-CPM statistics: Welch t 1243 genes
(620 overlapping, Spearman of p = 0.902), limma-style moderated t 1457 genes
(677 overlapping, Spearman of p = 0.938).

Leave-one-out (3 vs 2) sensitivity of the candidate set:
* drop KL3 -> 1000 candidates, Jaccard 0.643 vs full
* drop WL3 ->  868 candidates, Jaccard 0.681 vs full
Pathway-level leave-one-out sensitivity could NOT be assessed because enrichment never ran.

